content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22650",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the reported 4.8 mm/s at the drive end is numerically within Figure 3's Zone C range of 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS, for which the applicable instruction is 'Restricted - plan maintenance.' It exceeds the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/Zone C boundary but is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/Zone D boundary; it is therefore not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, and the immediate-stop rule is not triggered by this reading. This supports planned P2 corrective maintenance rather than an immediate stop. Figure 3's classification applies to RMS velocity measured on bearing housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the applicable HF-300 bearing-housing limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C, with temperature measured on the housing surface. The reported 70 C is exactly at the upper normal limit, 10 C below alarm and 20 C below trip. It is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so the SSP-07 requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no leakage is reported, so the troubleshooting symptom 'leakage at shaft seal' is not present. The evidence provides no numerical allowable leakage rate against which to make a quantitative comparison, and the report alone does not establish a need for mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is the first cause to check because the vibration began after motor replacement. The manual lists misalignment as a probable cause of high vibration and requires laser alignment after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is the next documented possibility; inspect the bearings rather than condemning them from vibration alone. The 70 C housing reading remains within the manual's normal range.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage is another documented cause of high vibration and requires inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is also a documented possible cause; the manual's corrective action includes checking NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before using the severity zones for final acceptance, verify and record the vibration as mm/s RMS measured on the bearing housing and record bearing temperature on the housing surface. Continue to manage the present 4.8 mm/s reading as Zone C restricted operation requiring planned maintenance; apply the immediate-stop control if a subsequent reading is classified in Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "First check and correct shaft alignment using a laser alignment tool following the motor replacement. The applicable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH to investigate the remaining documented causes: bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation. Record the inspection results before authorizing parts replacement beyond any condition-based bearing work below.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair using drive-end bearing HF3-512 and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510. Do not use the reported 70 C alone as a high-temperature replacement trigger because it is still within the documented normal range.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any authorized internal disassembly and reassembly, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. For lightly oiled threads, apply Table 5 where these fasteners are disturbed: M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts 210 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Do not apply the manual's generic 25 Nm seal-gland torque to this serial if seal work is added; the asset-specific bulletin decision in source_conflicts applies instead.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, restore the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. Recheck vibration and housing-surface temperature and compare them with Figure 3 and the 70/80/90 C temperature limits before closing the work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional only: supply as part of a bearing pair if inspection finds wear, noise or high temperature in either bearing; no bearing failure is yet confirmed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional only: replace together with HF3-512 when the pair-replacement criterion is met.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Required only if the casing is opened during authorized internal work; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. The mechanical-seal procedure likewise begins with isolation and draining.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is lifted for internal work, its documented mass is 68 kg and lifting equipment is required. Because this exceeds 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. Zone D is labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'; the current 4.8 mm/s reading is not in that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-housing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The documented trip limit is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry during restoration or testing.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Base-scope laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement, only if inspection triggers pair replacement: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number and gland torque conflict: the manual parts table lists component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives M10 seal-gland nuts 25 Nm, whereas SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, supersedes that seal for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and specifies 30 Nm. P-113 is serial HF3-22650, so it is inside the bulletin range. For any seal work on this asset, use the bulletin: do not fit HF3-450; fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement required, and tighten the gland nuts to 30 Nm. The instruction for pumps below HF3-22000 to continue using HF3-450 and Table 5 does not apply. No seal replacement is included in the base scope merely because of this conflict.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does the reported 4.8 mm/s represent RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing? Figure 3's zones expressly use that measurement basis, while the report only says 'at the drive end' (C07).",
    "What are the bearing condition and noise findings, impeller condition/balance findings, cavitation evidence and NPSH results? These determine whether the conditional bearings or any additional parts are actually required; no NPSH acceptance data are supplied (C09).",
    "No allowable numerical seal-leakage rate is documented, so 'no leakage' cannot be quantitatively compared with a leakage limit. The installed seal type and condition are also unknown; seal replacement should not be added without an inspection-based need (C09, C13).",
    "Is P-113 on a chemically dosed line? The dosing evidence identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line but does not establish P-113's service. Confirm this before deciding whether chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required (C15, C16).",
    "Table 6 gives no standard duration for the diagnostic bearing/impeller inspection, NPSH check, casing or impeller work, isolation, or final verification; those durations require site planning. Only alignment and conditional bearing replacement have documented labour standards (C12).",
    "Figure 3 does not state which zone owns values exactly on the 2.8, 4.5 or 7.1 mm/s boundaries. If a final reading falls exactly on a boundary, obtain clarification before using that boundary for acceptance or restart decisions (C07)."
  ]
}
